    <title>Ramanujan Series for Epstein Zeta Functions</title>
    <updated>2015-03-28T09:48:41Z</updated>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/abs/1410.8312v2" rel="alternate" type="text/html"/>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/pdf/1410.8312v2" rel="related" type="application/pdf" title="pdf"/>
    <summary>In the spirit of Ramanujan, we derive exponentially fast convergent series for Epstein zeta functions $ E^{\varGamma_0(N)}(z,s)$ on the Hecke congruence groups $ \varGamma_0(N),N\in\mathbb Z_{&gt;0}$, where $z$ is an arbitrary point in the upper half-plane $ \mathfrak H$, and $s\in\mathbb Z_{&gt;1}$. These Ramanujan series can be reformulated as integrations of modular forms, in the framework of Eichler integrals. Particular cases of these Eichler integrals recover part of the recent results reported by Wan and Zucker (arXiv:1410.7081v1).</summary>
