    <title>Epstein zeta-functions, subconvexity, and the purity conjecture</title>
    <updated>2016-02-07T01:11:43Z</updated>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/abs/1602.02326v1" rel="alternate" type="text/html"/>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/pdf/1602.02326v1" rel="related" type="application/pdf" title="pdf"/>
    <summary>Subconvexity bounds are proved for general Epstein zeta functions of k-ary quadratic forms. This is related to sup-norm bounds for Eisenstein series on GL(k), and the exact sup-norm exponent is determined to be (k-2)/8 for k &gt;= 2. In particular, if $k$ is odd, this exponent is not in Z/4, which shows that Sarnak's purity conjecture does not hold for Eisenstein series.</summary>
